[ ] Move calendar-sync policy from the filesystem adapter into Core =calendar-sync-into-core $filesystem/calendar.rs parses ICS and decides linking, migration matching and link cardinality before calling Core prepare_sync. Three layers: Plan domain owns link invariants; Core ICS/sync owns codec, UID evidence, roll-forward; adapter reads bytes and delivers effects. Needs a charter; the user drafts the outcome. Claim c41. After plan-link-sidecar-only.$ !2 ^2026-09-24T11:22 #01a0d4a7-f0bd-7465-8583-757b4b3e7dc1
[ ] Unify the three charter-stem derivations =unify-charter-stem $Core action_files.rs, nvim init.lua and cli/plan.rs disagree, e.g. on charters/next.actions and README.md. Keep one definition plus a shared conformance fixture that the Lua copy also tests against. Claim c42.$ !3 ^2026-09-24T11:22 #01a0d4a7-f0c4-775b-adcb-b7f6402d7e43
[ ] Report unresolved calendar sync conflicts in doctor =sync-conflicts-in-doctor $DECIDED 2026-09-24: doctor is the persistent view of workspace state. Warn per unresolved conflict with action, field and both values, plus the exact per-action resolution command. Never auto-fix: choosing a side is judgement. Transport health such as vdirsyncer stays out of ClearHead; staleness detection belongs to the scheduler.$ !3 ^2026-09-24T22:47 #01a0d71a-889a-73d3-aea7-d9720a0bb051
[ ] Rewrite the Radicale and vdirsyncer cookbook for unattended service =cookbook-unattended-sync $docs/cookbook/radicale-vdirsyncer.md teaches the three patterns that silently stopped the user's sync for two months: pass for an unattended service, where the gpg-agent cache caps at 24h; one chained oneshot where a transport failure also stops clearhead sync; and OnUnitActiveSec timers, which can end up never scheduled. Since 2026-09-24 sync exits 2 on unresolved conflicts, so a chained oneshot would also halt vdirsyncer on every conflict, another reason to split the units. Document the working setup: a systemd-creds credential decrypted by the vdirsyncer password.fetch command, separate clearhead-sync and vdirsyncer units on staggered OnCalendar timers, and OnFailure hooks that treat exit 2 as needs a decision rather than broken.$ !3 ^2026-09-24T22:47 #01a0d71a-88a1-7319-b7f2-0b7964cfb13a
[=] Make CI pass --locked against the committed Cargo.lock $NEEDS DECISION: how should the platform grammar patch and a standalone Cargo.lock coexist? CI has failed on every push to main since at least run 206, and most likely since about 2026-08-21, when --locked came in: the Clippy step stops with cannot update the lock file because --locked was passed (run 36115296096, 2026-09-25). Cause: platform .cargo/config.toml patches the tree-sitter-actions git dependency to the sibling submodule, so every Cargo.lock written inside the platform tree records tree-sitter-actions as a path package with no source. Every committed lock back to 2026-08-21 has that shape. A standalone checkout such as CI resolves the git rev instead and must rewrite the lock. The test steps never run, so CI also hides test failures such as the time-zone snapshot bug. Note that the two pins also differ: Cargo.toml pins grammar rev 32f7f6f while platform pins the submodule at de45e62, so the standalone and platform builds are not the same code. Options: (a) CI rebuilds the platform composition: check out the grammar at the pinned rev beside core and write the same patch, so the committed lock is the one CI verifies. (b) Commit a standalone lock with the git source; but every in-platform build rewrites the lock, so the tree stays dirty and the platform shape keeps getting committed back, which is how this happened. (c) Drop --locked in CI; loses lock reproducibility. (d) Retire the platform patch and bump the rev pin when the grammar changes; local grammar work then needs a temporary patch.$ !2 ^2026-09-25T17:56 #01a0d9b6-2e52-7ab0-9bc1-0f4ae5ca4869
[ ] Scaffold the union merge driver for completed actions =completed-union-merge $Completed actions are append-only facts, so two branches that each complete an action conflict only because both appended at the end of the same file. Git's built-in union driver keeps both sides: .clearhead/.gitattributes with the line *.completed.actions merge=union. It must not cover next.actions, where a completed action has to disappear. Platform and clearhead-core carry it since 2026-09-25, found while landing parallel sandbox runs. Remaining: clearhead init writes it beside the .gitignore it already creates, and the other platform submodules with a .clearhead get it.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T16:00 #01a0dacc-c415-70c0-9bdd-d4ac4302097c
[ ] Cross-workspace --charter resolution falls back to a title substring match before failing $resolve_charter_across_workspaces / resolve_markdown_charter falls back to a case-insensitive title-substring match across ALL loaded workspaces before reporting NotFound. Querying --charter ontology from the platform root can silently match platform's own someday/application-ontology charter (title contains ontology) instead of the ontology submodule's own root, with no error and no indication of the mismatch — only reproducible by noticing the query returns 0 rows when the target charter has none either. Found while verifying materialize-implicit-charters (01a0dab7). Fix: prefer an exact alias/title match across all workspaces before falling back to substring match in any of them.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T23:23 #01a0dae1-7f23-7cd3-91cd-a81247d8c670
[ ] Move an action to another charter =move-action-between-charters $Found 2026-09-25 while parking the support charter: no verb moves an action between charters keeping its id. update action --charter only scopes the lookup. Workarounds lose identity, delete then add, or bypass the CLI with a hand edit of two .actions files. A move should carry the line, its children and its sidecar state, keeping the UUID.$ !3 ^2026-09-25T16:51 #01a0dafb-2037-7302-8099-77a95be083b8
[ ] Make lint CLI tests write their fixtures to a temp dir $Found 2026-09-30: tests/lint_cli.rs (test_lint_cli_success, test_lint_cli_info_diagnostics) write test_*.actions into the crate directory, so they fail in a read-only checkout (a sandbox review session) and leave files in the source tree if interrupted. Use tempfile like the other CLI tests.$ !4 ^2026-09-30T14:50 #01a0f44c-58a0-752e-a856-7a16b88781ef
